### D05–D07 — Camera Geometry Before Threshold Tuning

**Problem:**  
Earlier vision behaviour could not be made sufficiently reliable through threshold adjustment alone.

**Key finding:**  

> A colour threshold cannot detect information that the camera does not see clearly.

**Previous approach:**

```text
Detection problem
      ↓
Adjust threshold
      ↓
Adjust threshold again
```

**Revised approach:**

```text
Detection problem
      ↓
Inspect raw camera view
      ↓
Check camera geometry
      ↓
Check useful field of view
      ↓
Redesign camera position / mount
      ↓
Define task-specific ROIs
      ↓
Calibrate thresholds
```

**Decision:**  
Redesign the camera configuration and build the vision pipeline around **multiple task-specific ROIs**.

This changed the design question from:

> "Which pixels have the correct colour?"

to:

> "Which relevant pixels, in the correct part of the image, have the correct colour for the robot's current state?"

That distinction became fundamental to the final perception architecture.

