### D16–D18 — Why Parking Became Multi-Sensor

Parking requires information about several different physical quantities.

| Required Information | Sensor / Method |
| --- | --- |
| Visual course cue | Camera |
| Robot orientation | MPU6050 / heading |
| Local physical gap | ToF sensors |
| Vehicle movement | Encoder where applicable |

The earlier architecture relied more heavily on **camera interpretation and heading**.

That was sufficient for determining:

- what the robot could see;
- approximately where it was in the sequence;
- which direction it was facing.

It did **not** directly answer:

> "How far is the robot from the nearby physical surface?"

The final architecture therefore added ToF sensing.

```text
Camera
   ↓
Course / parking context

IMU
   ↓
Heading / orientation

ToF sensors
   ↓
Physical distance

Encoder
   ↓
Vehicle displacement

        ↓
Combined parking decision
```

The additional complexity was accepted because the sensors answer different questions rather than merely duplicating one another.

