## Examples of Rejected or Replaced Approaches

Engineering decisions are also visible through approaches that were deliberately **not** retained.

| Rejected / Replaced Approach | Reason It Was Not Retained |
| --- | --- |
| Aggressive speed-increasing drivetrain gearing | Reduced torque and reliability margin |
| Purely time-based precision movement | Sensitive to changing physical conditions |
| Large unrestricted steering corrections | Risk of mechanical stress |
| Threshold-only solution to poor camera geometry | Software could not compensate for missing visual information |
| Whole-frame or overly broad colour detection | Increased irrelevant detections |
| Immediate action from one visual cue | Created premature state transitions |
| Parking based mainly on vision and timing | Did not directly measure physical distance |
| One distance sample as a parking trigger | Susceptible to transient readings |
| Identical CW and ACW parking entry | Different physical approach geometry |
| Full-system-only debugging | Difficult to isolate the originating failure |
| Retaining Nationals architecture through tuning alone | Some limitations required architectural changes |

